          "title": "Black smoke under acceleration - treated as a DPF issue, not injectors.",
          "description": "The fleet manager first noticed black smoke from the Transit under acceleration. The driver reported a gradual loss of power, particularly up hills. The van failed its MOT on emissions. An independent garage diagnosed a clogged DPF and failing EGR valve.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/case-studies/assets/1.2-ford-transit-22-wasted-receipts.png",
