    "diagnosis": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "the-specialist-confirmed-failed-injectors-bore-wash-and-scored-cylinders",
          "title": "The specialist confirmed failed injectors, bore wash, and scored cylinders.",
          "description": "The specialist performed a compression test, injector leak-off test, and borescope inspection. The findings were severe - the engine needed a full rebuild or replacement.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.1-ford-transit-22-failed-injectors.png",
              "alt": "Ford 2.2 Duratorq leak-off test showing failed injectors on cylinders 2 and 3",
              "width": "",
              "height": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.2-ford-transit-22-bore-wash-scoring.png",
              "alt": "Ford 2.2 Duratorq cylinder bore scoring from bore wash caused by failed injectors",
              "width": "",
              "height": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.3-ford-transit-22-dpf-clogged.png",
              "alt": "Ford Transit 2.2 DPF clogged after 3 months due to failed injectors over-fuelling",
              "width": "",
              "height": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Injectors (cylinders 2 & 3)"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Failed - excessive leak-off, poor spray pattern"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Piston rings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Worn - bore wash damage, excessive oil consumption"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Cylinder bores"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Scoring visible on cylinder 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "DPF"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Rapidly clogging again - ash load high despite new unit"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "EGR valve"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Carboned up"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Turbocharger"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Unknown condition - possible oil contamination from blow-by"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Specialist summary"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "\"The injectors failed first. They've been over-fuelling for months. That killed the DPF and EGR, and it's worn the rings and bores. You can replace the injectors and rings, but the bores are scored. This engine needs a full rebuild or replacement. The £1,200 you spent on the DPF and EGR was wasted - the injectors killed them again.\""
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Repair options"
            }
